<HelpChapterSection Id="profile">
    <HelpTopicSection Id="profile-overview">
        <p>Open <span class="help-ui">Profile</span> in the menu or click your name at the bottom of the side menu. The profile has three tabs: <span class="help-ui">Profile</span>, <span class="help-ui">Security</span> and <span class="help-ui">Sessions</span>.</p>
        <p>On the <span class="help-ui">Profile</span> tab:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Card</strong> — full name, email, the <span class="help-ui">2FA enabled</span> badge and the time of your last sign-in.</li>
            <li><strong>Positions</strong> — all your positions: title, unit and role. Your primary position is marked <span class="help-ui">Primary</span>. Click a position to open the unit's page. If you have no positions — “No positions assigned. Contact the HR department.”</li>
            <li><strong>Available modules</strong> — the modules of the cabinet open to you. Expand <span class="help-ui">All my permissions</span> to see each permission with its description.</li>
            <li><strong>Contacts</strong> — your email (cannot be changed, it is your login) and <span class="help-ui">Phone</span>. Enter the number in the +380… format and click <span class="help-ui">Save</span> — “Phone number saved.” appears.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Your name and positions are managed by the HR department. If the data is wrong or you lack access to a module, contact them or the system administrator.</p>
        <p><strong>Interface language.</strong> The cabinet is available in Ukrainian and English. In the <span class="help-ui">Interface language</span> card, choose <span class="help-ui">Українська</span> or <span class="help-ui">English</span> and click <span class="help-ui">Apply</span>. The language is saved in your profile and applies on all your devices. Before signing in, you can change the language with the button in the top-right corner of the sign-in page.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="profile-security">
        <p>The <span class="help-ui">Security</span> tab has three cards.</p>
        <h4>Password</h4>
        <p>The <span class="help-ui">Change password</span> button opens the password change form (see “<a href="/help#account-change-password">Changing your password</a>”).</p>
        <h4>Two-factor authentication</h4>
        <p>Shows the status: <span class="help-ui">Enabled</span> or <span class="help-ui">Not set up</span>. Changed your phone? Ask the administrator to reset your authenticator — you will set up the new one the next time you sign in.</p>
        <h4>Recovery codes</h4>
        <p>Shows how many codes are left. If you are running low on codes or suspect someone has seen them, generate a new set:</p>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Open the authenticator app and enter the current 6-digit code in the field next to the <span class="help-ui">New codes</span> button. This is an extra confirmation: without your phone the codes cannot be changed, even with an open session.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">New codes</span> and confirm “Generate new codes? The old ones will stop working.”</li>
            <li>10 new codes appear. Click <span class="help-ui">Copy</span> and save them — they will not be shown again. The old codes no longer work.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>A wrong code shows the message “The code is incorrect or has already been used. Enter the next code from the app.” Wrong codes count towards the failed attempts limit (5 attempts — blocked for 15 minutes).</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="profile-sessions">
        <p>The <span class="help-ui">Sessions</span> tab shows all devices you are signed in from: <span class="help-ui">Device</span> (browser and operating system), <span class="help-ui">IP address</span>, the time of sign-in (<span class="help-ui">Signed in</span>) and of the last activity (<span class="help-ui">Activity</span>). The session you are working in now is marked <span class="help-ui">Current session</span>.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><span class="help-ui">End</span> in a session's row ends that one session (after the “End this session?” confirmation): a new sign-in will be needed on that device. The current session cannot be ended this way — sign out of the cabinet instead.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">End all others</span> — after the “End all other sessions?” confirmation, ends all sessions except the current one and shows “Sessions ended: N”. Useful if you forgot to sign out on someone else's computer or see an unfamiliar device.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Ended sessions stop working immediately, including pages still open on those devices. If you see a session you don't recognize, end it and change your password.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>
</HelpChapterSection>
